.TH CLOG_REMOVE_FIELD 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
clog_remove_field \- remove a previously attached structured field
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <clogger.h>

void clog_remove_field(clog logger, const char *key);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Removes the field with the given key from the logger's field list.
The field will no longer appear in subsequent log lines. If the key
is not present the call is a no-op.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
logger  Logger handle.
key     Field name to remove. The match is case-sensitive and exact.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Thread-safe: protected by the per-logger mutex.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR clog_set_field (3),
.BR clog_clear_fields (3)
